{
  "$comment": [
    "Spoken punctuation and layout commands (#294), per language (BCP 47",
    "primary subtag). A mode with spoken_commands true uses the table of its",
    "language; an undeclared language (null) uses 'en'; a language without a",
    "table gets no commands. Matching is whole-token and case-insensitive,",
    "ignoring punctuation the recognizer attached to the command word",
    "(,.;:!?); a quoted mention never matches. The literal word before a",
    "command keeps the command as plain text ('literal new line').",
    "Actions: punctuation attaches value to the previous word (replacing",
    "punctuation the recognizer already put there); line_break and",
    "paragraph insert a newline / blank line and drop the spaces around it;",
    "bullet starts a '- ' list item on its own line.",
    "Semantics: tests/spoken_commands.py; fixtures/spoken-commands.json."
  ],
